# Local development overrides for `astro dev`.
#
# Copy to `.dev.vars` and edit. That file is gitignored and must never be
# committed - this repository is public, so a committed secret could not be
# unpublished.
#
# There are no secrets here today, and that is the point rather than an
# oversight: this Worker has no database, no provider credentials and no API
# keys. If a value you are about to add here is one you would not want read by
# a stranger, it almost certainly belongs in the backend instead.

# Where the backend is, for local development only.
#
# Deployed, the site reaches the backend over a Cloudflare service binding and
# this variable is ignored entirely - `resolveTransport` in src/middleware.ts
# honors it only when ENVIRONMENT is `development`, so a staging or production
# deployment that somehow acquired it would still use its binding. Without that
# guard this would be a way to point the live site at any origin.
#
# Two useful values:
#
#   http://localhost:8788  the fake backend in scripts/fake-backend.ts, which
#                          needs no private repository and no credentials, and
#                          can be put into failure modes on demand
#
#   http://localhost:4322  a real local backend from the private repository,
#                          started with its own `pnpm dev` on that port
#
# Leave it unset to develop against a backend that is not there, which renders
# the failure states. Those are worth looking at more often than they are.
BACKEND_DEV_URL=http://localhost:8788

# Where the media route reads image bytes, for local development only.
#
# The media route proxies provider images so the browser never contacts a
# provider network. `resolveMediaOrigin` in src/middleware.ts honors this only
# when ENVIRONMENT is `development`, for the reason stated above BACKEND_DEV_URL:
# without that guard this would point the live site's media route at any origin.
#
# scripts/fake-backend.ts serves real image bytes from tests/fixtures/media/ for
# every image address the recorded corpus carries. So this is the same process
# BACKEND_DEV_URL names, on the same port.
#
# Leave it unset to fetch from the real provider host instead.
MEDIA_DEV_URL=http://localhost:8788
